  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/3F1C0A">Remark <span data-tag="3F1C0A">7.1.6.10</span>.</a> Let $\ast $ denote a topological space consisting of a single point. By definition, $\Shv (\ast )$ is the full subcategory of $\Fun (\Delta ^1,\SSet )$ spanned by those morphisms $f: X \rightarrow Y$ where $Y$ is a final object of $\SSet $. We observe that $\Shv (\ast )$ is equivalent to the full subcategory spanned by those morphisms $f$ as above where $Y = \Delta ^0 \in \SSet $, and that this full subcategory is <em>isomorphic</em> to $\SSet $. </p>
